-- title:
--   Adapted corner-lattice basis from an involution and a similitude
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $T$ a finite free $\mathbb Z_p$-module, equipped with a family $A : \iota_0 \to \operatorname{End}_{\mathbb Z_p}(T)$ and with an action of a commutative $\mathbb Z_p$-algebra $\mathbb T$ compatible with the $\mathbb Z_p$-structure, such that the action is faithful (any $t \in \mathbb T$ killing all of $T$ is $0$), and such that for a map $\mathrm{op} : \iota_0 \to \mathbb T$ one has $\mathrm{op}(g) \cdot x = A_g x$ for all $g, x$, with $\mathbb T$ generated as a $\mathbb Z_p$-algebra by the image of $\mathrm{op}$. Let $S'$ be an idempotent splitting of $\mathbb T$, that is, a number $n$, complete orthogonal idempotents $e_0,\dots,e_{n-1}$ and maximal ideals $\mathfrak m_i$ exhausting the maximal ideals of $\mathbb T$ with $e_i \in \mathfrak m_j \iff i \ne j$; fix an index $i_0$, write $e = e_{i_0}$, let $P = eT$ be the corner submodule (the image of multiplication by $e$ on $T$) and let $A_0$ denote the corner ring of $e$, whose elements act on $T$ through their image in $\mathbb T$. Assume $2$ is a unit in $\mathbb Z_p$, let $s_0, t_1 \in \operatorname{End}_{\mathbb Z_p}(T)$ commute with the $\mathbb T$-action, let $u \in \mathbb Z_p$, and let $P_0$ be a $\mathbb T$-submodule of $T$ whose elements are exactly the $x \in P$ with $s_0 x = -x$; assume $s_0^2 = \mathrm{id}$ on $P$, that $t_1 x = u x$ for $x \in P_0$, and that $t_1 x - x \in P_0$ for $x \in P$. Rationally, assume $V = \mathbb Q_p \otimes_{\mathbb Z_p} T$ admits a basis indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,2$ over the $\mathbb Q_p$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}(V)$ generated by the base changes of the $A_g$, and let $B$ be a $\mathbb Q_p$-bilinear form on $V$ such that $B(x,\,\cdot\,) = 0$ forces $x = 0$, each base-changed $A_g$ is self-adjoint for $B$, and $B(t_1x, t_1y) = u\,B(x,y)$, with $u(u-1) \ne 0$ in $\mathbb Q_p$. The conclusion is the existence of $x_0 \in P_0$, of $y \in P$ with $s_0 y = y$, and of $N \in \mathbb N$ such that $x_0$ and $y$ are $A_0$-independent (if $a x_0 + b y = 0$ with $a,b \in A_0$ then $a = b = 0$), $p^N P \subseteq A_0 x_0 + A_0 y$, $p^N P_0 \subseteq A_0 x_0$, and $p^N z \in A_0 y$ for every $z \in P$ with $s_0 z = z$.
--
--   This is the abstract lattice-theoretic form of the rank-and-index step in the analysis of the ordinary filtration in Wiles, Chapter 2 §1: a corner $eT$ of a $p$-adic lattice carrying a commutative Hecke action, an involution and an operator scaling a non-degenerate pairing by a factor $u$ with $u(u-1) \neq 0$, is shown to contain, up to a bounded power of $p$, a free rank-two piece adapted to the $\pm$-eigenspaces of the involution. It is applied with $T$ the $p$-adic Tate module of a modular Jacobian, $s_0$ and $t_1$ the images of suitable inertia elements and the Fricke-twisted Weil pairing, to obtain [`ModularCurve.exists_adaptedLatticeBasis_inertiaEigenspace_cornerSubmodule_tateModule_jH_of_ordinary`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_adaptedLatticeBasis_inertiaEigenspace_cornerSubmodule_tateModule_jH_of_ordinary).
